package CanvasNet {
    part def FeatureCatalog {
        doc /* The internal static FeatureCatalog with the FeatureReport record and the FeatureReportKind enumeration: a pure function of the parsed SpecTree that lists every construct of a Vega-Lite specification that the renderer recognizes but does not implement, each with a stable lower-case vl- identifier (vl-schema-version, vl-data-*, vl-mark-type, vl-channel-name, vl-type-*, vl-scale-*, vl-encoding-*, vl-guide-*, vl-format-type-custom, vl-expr-*, vl-transform-name, vl-composition-*, vl-param-*, vl-projection, vl-layout-autosize-*) and the exact location, sorted by line and column with a stable sort. Phase 5 removes the reports of the supported expressions and transforms (vl-expr-calculate, vl-expr-filter, and vl-transform-calculate, filter, fold, flatten, sample, pivot, and lookup of the drawn view, vl-param-variable of the drawn view, and vl-expr-ref at the row-bound sites) and adds vl-expr-function-name (a function outside the whitelist, the name lower-cased in the identifier and as written in the message), vl-expr-view-state (signal, event, item, and undeclared width, height, padding, autosize, background, or cursor), vl-expr-construct-name (bitwise and shift operators and in), each at the expression string with the offset in the message, plus vl-transform-filter-param, vl-transform-filter-timeunit, vl-transform-filter-datetime, vl-transform-pivot-op, and vl-transform-lookup-param for the parts of supported transforms that are not executed; Phase 6 removes the reports of the supported grouping transforms and encodings (vl-transform-aggregate, joinaggregate, window, bin, stack, and impute of the drawn view, vl-encoding-aggregate, vl-encoding-stack, vl-encoding-bin of x and y, vl-encoding-sort of the supported forms, vl-channel-x2 and vl-channel-y2 of bar, rect, and rule marks, and vl-channel-order when it orders an active stack, decided with the StackRules of the Transforms subsystem) and adds vl-encoding-bin-extent-param and vl-transform-bin-extent-param (an extent given by a parameter, ignored) and vl-encoding-stack-nonlinear (an explicit stack on a scale that is not linear); the transforms timeunit, regression, loess, density, quantile, and extent, every transform and variable parameter of a nested view, the encoding impute (vl-encoding-impute), selection parameters, conditional encodings (vl-encoding-condition), bin on a channel other than x and y (vl-encoding-bin), and the channel sorts that are not ascending, descending, null, a value list, an encoding sort, or an aggregate object (vl-encoding-sort) stay reported. It is the single definition of the supported boundary: supported marks, channels, scale types, scale properties, and data sources are absent from its result. It classifies a data url as remote (a scheme, drive letter, absolute path, or network path: vl-data-remote-url, never fetched; a relative local path is supported and not reported), reports a custom parse date format as vl-data-parse-date-format and text or object datasets as vl-data-values-text or vl-data-geo, chooses a data source by precedence rather than key order, and reports an empty or sourceless data object as the warning vl-data-empty; it opens no file, reads no data rows, and uses no network. The identifiers vl-data-file, vl-data-named, vl-data-sequence, vl-data-parse, vl-data-format-*, and vl-data-property are retired (their constructs are supported). The warnings vl-duplicate-key and vl-unknown-property are produced by the SpecParser unit. */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/FeatureCatalog.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/FeatureCatalogTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/feature-catalog.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/feature-catalog.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/feature-catalog.yaml */
    }
}
